  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "FOR THE ROASTED CHICKEN & VEGGIES: Preheat oven to 400°F.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, peel, and medium dice sweet potatoes. Peel, halve, and slice onions lengthwise into ¼-inch thick strips. Divide sweet potato, onion, and cauliflower between two baking sheet pans.",
      "secondary_message": "454 g sweet potato\n2 (283 g) bag cauliflower florets"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Large dice chicken. Add to the baking sheets with the veggies, then drizzle with oil and sprinkle with spices. Stir to combine and spread out in an even layer.",
      "secondary_message": "907 g chicken thighs, boneless skinless\n¼ cup extra virgin olive oil\n1 tbsp pumpkin spice mix\n1 ½ tsp cumin, ground\n1 tsp salt\n½ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking sheets in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and roast, stirring halfway, until veggies are fork-tender and chicken is cooked through, about 40 minutes. Remove from oven and set aside to cool slightly, about 5 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "FOR THE SALAD: While the chicken and veggies are cooling, wash and dry the spinach (skip this step if it came pre-washed). Place in a large bowl.",
      "secondary_message": "2 (142 g) pkg baby spinach"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using a clean cutting board, roughly chop apricots and pistachios. Add both to the bowl with the spinach, along with dressing, then toss to combine the salad.",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup pistachios, unsalted\n⅓ cup lemon garlic vinaigrette"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide salad between plates or bowls, then top with roasted chicken and veggies. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
